ain, and Interiors Studio Director and supports the overall success and high caliber of projects within the Interiors Studio by contributing excellence in design and production efforts.\n\nThe hiring salary range for this position is $75,000 – $105,000. Any offer of compensation will be determined by a candidate’s education, skills, and experience as assessed during the interview process."}, {"h": "Job Responsibilities", "t": "Perform the daily functions that support a successful project throughout design development, budgeting and procurement, and final installation.\nMeet and communicate directly with consultants and vendors\nClose coordination with architectural, landscape, and construction studios within the Office as required.\nProduce cohesive, accurate, and beautiful furniture plans, interior elevations, interior 3D views, client presentations, and custom furniture drawings as directed\nMeet regularly with Interiors Project Manager and Interiors Job Captain to review project progress and assigned tasks.\nPerform all tasks with diligence, high attention to detail, and according to Interiors Studio and Office standards\n\nRequired Skills\n\nA Bachelor’s Degree or equivalent education in Interior Design at an accredited institution\n2-5 years of relevant industry experience with an exceptional reputation\nVery strong communication, design, and organizational skills\nTechnical skills: Revit, Adobe Creative Suite, Sketchup, Microsoft Excel, Design Manager, Lumion\nThe ability to communicate openly and positively with colleagues and partners at all times\nA positive outlook and strong work ethic\n\nTo apply, please email your cover letter, resume, and work samples (academic and professional) as a single PDF no larger than 5 MB to employment@marmol-radziner.com. No links to portfolios please.\n\nDue to the high volume of resumes we receive, we are only able to respond to those we are interested in interviewing. No telephone calls please.\n\narchitecture\nconstruction\nlandscape\ninteriors\nprefab\nfabrication\nhome goods\nfurniture\nabout\nthe firm\ndesign/build\npeople\ncareers\nawards\npress\ncontact\nsearch"}], "k": ["budgeting", "excel", "lumion", "presentation", "procurement", "revit", "sketchup", "supply-chain"], "r": {"exp": 2, "edu": {"level": "bachelor", "state": "waived"}}}, "d09bafa6fe": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Skip to content"}, {"h": "CONTACT", "t": "Senior Interior Designers\n\nWe are growing and looking for talented and experienced Senior Interior Designers to join our London studio and work on a range of different typologies around the world.\n\nAt Conran and Partners, you’ll work across a wide variety of sectors, scales and geographies – from hospitality and residential to commercial – collaborating with our international team of architects and interior designers."}, {"h": "THE ROLE", "t": "We are looking for senior interior designers with proven experience and design sensibilities that sit well with our studio ethos to support new projects in the hospitality, residential and commercial sectors.\n\nThe ideal candidate will have 5+ years of experience with creative drive and technical understanding.\n\nApplicants should have a flair for design and experience working on high-quality projects demonstrated through a beautiful portfolio of work, exhibiting their ability to contribute to the design sensibilities of the practice."}, {"h": "ABOUT YOU", "t": "Minimum 5+ years’ experience working on design-led projects"}, {"h": "Interior design degree or architectural qualifications", "t": "Strong background in the hospitality, high-end residential or workplace sectors\nClient facing with proven experience of job running\nCreative flair, conceptual approach\nUnderstanding of and experience in delivering pitches to drawing packages and schedules\nStrong knowledge and practical experience of AutoCAD or Revit, Sketchup, Rhino and Enscape. 3D rendering abilities.\nStrong graphic communication and presentation skills, InDesign and Photoshop experience is essential.\nExperience leading and managing people, as well as mentoring junior members\nA good knowledge of finishes and FF+E specification along with a desire to continually source new and interesting products.\nExperience working in Asia and fluency in either Mandarin, Cantonese and Japanese is a plus.\n\nThis is a full-time position. All candidates should be eligible to work in the UK.\n\nConran and Partners is an equal opportunities employer and offers the opportunity for growth. We recognise the lack of diversity in our industry, and encourage applicants from under-represented backgrounds to apply. Other benefits include flexible working."}, {"h": "HOW TO APPLY", "t": "Please apply in writing including a CV, portfolio and accompanying letter stating both current and expected salaries to: recruitment@conran.com and clearly mark the subject heading ‘Senior Interior Designer, London’.\n\nPlease note that only successful candidates will be contacted.\n\nWe look forward to hearing from you!"}, {"h": "SHARE", "t": "© 2026. All rights reserved. Website design by NexusBond"}], "k": ["autocad", "enscape", "indesign", "photoshop", "presentation", "rendering", "revit", "rhino", "sketchup", "training"], "r": {"exp": 5, "lang": ["Mandarin", "Japanese"]}}, "b70bf6f543": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Skip to Content\nSearch Jobs\nRecommended Jobs\nCareers\nEnglish (United States)\nSign In\nSr Project Interior Designer\nReq #649\nLos Angeles, CA, USA\nApply\nShare\nJob Description\nPosted Thursday, August 6, 2026 at 7:00 AM\n\nHOK is a collective of future-forward thinkers and designers who are driven to face the critical challenges of our time. We are dedicated to improving people's lives, serving our clients and healing the planet. Together, we cultivate a culture of design excellence at the confluence of art and science, blending the power of creative expression with a clear sense of purpose.\n\nResponsible for interpreting, organizing and executing the conceptual design of a project. Utilizes creativity, foresight and judgment to meet project requirements and objectives to carry out design.\n\nTo perform in this position successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.\n\nHOK is a collective of future-forward thinkers and designers who are driven to face the critical challenges of our time. We are dedicated to improving people's lives, serving our clients and healing the planet. Together, we cultivate a culture of design excellence at the confluence of art and science, blending the power of creative expression with a clear sense of purpose.\n\nIn partnership with the Sr. Project Manager and Sr. Project Architect, accountable for project financial performance and team communication. As a member of the project team, establishes overall design direction, develops architectural design concepts and prepares documents during the design development phase.\n\nResponsible for the development of conceptual design of all phases of one or more projects. Assists and coordinates with the construction document preparation to support design intent, prepares for design presentations and coordinates with agencies affecting design.\n\nAt HOK, we are a collective of future‑forward designers, thinkers, and makers united by a shared ambition: to shape a healthier, more sustainable, and more inspiring built environment. We believe great design emerges from creativity, curiosity, rigorous thinking, and a deep sense of purpose.\n\nOur teams thrive at the intersection of art and science where bold ideas meet technical mastery, and where design has the power to improve lives and heal the planet. We are seeking a Senior Project Interior Designer who shares our passion for design excellence and meaningful impact.\n\nThis role is ideal for a creative leader who excels at developing strong design concepts, collaborating across disciplines, and guiding teams toward exceptional project outcomes."}, {"h": "WHAT YOU’LL DO", "t": "As a key member of the project team, the Senior Project interior Designer:\n\nLeads overall design direction with guidance from the Design Director or Design Principal, shaping the conceptual vision for one or more projects from early exploration through design development.\nDevelops and advances architectural design concepts, ensuring work reflects HOK’s high standards of innovation, sustainability, and technical rigor.\nWorks collaboratively with project architects, managers, and consultants to translate design intent into coordinated construction documents.\nPrepares and delivers compelling design presentations, communicating ideas with clarity and storytelling that inspire clients and stakeholders.\nCoordinates with agencies and regulatory bodies, ensuring alignment between design excellence and compliance requirements.\nPartners closely with the Senior Project Manager and Senior Project Architect to support seamless project delivery, strong team communication, and responsible financial performance.\nChampions sustainable thinking, integrating environmental responsibility as an essential component of design quality"}, {"h": "RESPONSIBILITIES", "t": "Conducts programming efforts such as space planning, layout and utilization of furnishings and equipment, lighting and color coordination.\nDevelops innovative design concepts which are practical, aesthetic, safe and conducive to intended purposes and function which is reflective of client goals and within project budget.\nCoordinates color and material palettes.\nResponsible for selection and specification of furniture, lighting, flooring, wall covering and artwork. Estimates material requirements and preliminary costs.\nIncorporates Integrated Sustainable Design solutions into projects.\nRenders conceptual design ideas and prepares 2D and 3D presentation/design drawings.\nPrepares and conducts client presentations.\nPrepares, corrects and updates documents during schematic design and design development phases.\nSolicits bids and assists Project Manager and client in subcontracting fabrication, installation, and arrangement of the materials, finishes, and furnishings required.\nResponsible for keeping the project, or a phase of a project, on schedule.\nResponsible for communication with other disciplines, vendors, and contractors to ensure incorporation of all information into project requirements and provides support as necessary.\nSupports the Construction Administration phase responding to RFI’s, CO’s, and reviews shop drawings.\nImplements and utilizes HOK Standards for all projects and processes.\nMay provide support to all team members for specific field, style, or phase of interior design expertise.\nMay mentor and direct the work of less experienced staff and deliver staff performance evaluations.\nMay participate in interviews and recruiting of professional staff.\nTakes personal responsibility for fostering a green workplace through sustainable work practices.\nFosters a commitment to external and internal client service."}, {"h": "EDUCATION & EXPERIENCE", "t": "Requires a Bachelor’s degree in architecture, interior design or foreign equivalent\n10 plus years’ experience in interiors projects required.\nMust be a professional Interior Designer and have passed the NCIDQ exam or be a registered Architect with current license required."}, {"h": "LEED accreditation or Green Associate preferred.", "t": "Many of our roles require the use of specific software. Please refer to the Required and Preferred Software & Skills for details.\n\nHOK invests in its people and communities, supporting both personal and professional growth through every stage of life. At HOK you’ll have a hybrid work environment, 10 paid holidays (including 2 floating holidays) and a minimum of 4 weeks of paid time off with a cash out option.\n\nHOK offers comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, free mental wellness resources, life and AD&D coverage and short and long-term disability benefits. HOK supports your growing family by offering 4 weeks of paid parental leave and fertility coverage.\n\nHOK helps to fund your future financial needs with matching contributions to our 401(K) plan which includes a well-rounded investment menu as well as free guidance on retirement planning.\n\nWherever you are in your career, HOK provides opportunities to learn, develop and utilize your skills. Continued learning is promoted through financial support and study prep for licensure exams, CEU credit opportunities, mentorship programs, and paid professional memberships. To learn more about designing your career with HOK, explore our current job openings."}], "k": ["accessibility", "cad-drafting", "construction-administration", "construction-documents", "data-analysis", "jira", "leed", "materials", "presentation", "project-management", "rendering", "space-planning", "sustainability", "writing"], "b": ["bonus", "certification-support", "fertility", "generous-pto", "life-insurance", "mentorship", "parental-leave", "vision"], "r": {"exp": 10, "edu": {"level": "bachelor", "state": "required"}}}, "8007e0f139": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Michael Hsu Office Of Architecture\nCatalogue\n\nStudio\n\nPeople\n\nMerit\n\nMedia\n\nJoin\n\nDesign for All\ncontact\n\ninfo@hsuoffice.com\n512.706.4303\n\naustin\n\n826 Houston Street, Suite 100\nAustin, Texas 78756\n\nhouston\n\n1906 Ashland Street\nHouston, Texas 77008\n\nthroughout\n\nAtlanta, Boston, Denver, and Philadelphia\n\nfollow\n\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\n\nback\nInterior Designer\nAustin, TX\n—\n\nMichael Hsu Office of Architecture is an award-winning, fully integrated architecture and interior design practice with offices in Austin and Houston.\n\nOur work is rooted in hospitality and placemaking and includes diverse projects that range from large mixed-use developments, adaptive reuse projects, public realm design, architectural branding, single family homes, hotels, restaurants, workspaces, and bespoke furniture design.\n\nWe work throughout Texas and across the country in cities such as New York, Los Angeles, Chicago, Atlanta and Denver."}, {"h": "About the Position", "t": "We are seeking an experienced Interior Designer to join our Austin office. This role is ideal for a designer who is ready to take ownership of meaningful portions of a project while continuing to grow their technical, design, and project leadership skills. Working alongside experienced project leaders and design teams, this individual will contribute to projects across a variety of scales and typologies, helping translate design concepts into thoughtful, well-executed spaces and experiences.\n\nThe ideal candidate brings a strong foundation in interior design, a passion for creating memorable environments, and a desire to contribute to both the creative and technical aspects of project delivery. They are comfortable collaborating across disciplines, communicating clearly with team members and consultants, and managing their work with increasing independence and accountability.\n\nThis is a hybrid position based in Austin, TX, requiring a minimum of three days per week working in person from our Austin office."}, {"h": "Responsibilities Include", "t": "Contributing to the design and delivery of projects across a variety of scales, typologies, and phases of design\nDeveloping interior design concepts and translating them into coordinated drawings, details, renderings, presentations, and construction documents\nCreating mood boards, finish palettes, material studies, and presentation materials that communicate design intent clearly and effectively\nAssisting with the selection, specification, and coordination of finishes, fixtures, furnishings, artwork, and accessories\nContributing to the design and coordination of custom furniture, millwork, lighting, and other bespoke interior elements\nCoordinating with consultants, vendors, and internal team members to maintain project alignment and documentation quality\nSupporting construction administration efforts, including responding to RFIs, reviewing submittals, and assisting with field observations\nTaking ownership of assigned portions of a project while proactively communicating progress, questions, and potential coordination issues\nParticipating on multiple concurrent projects in various capacities"}, {"h": "Job Requirements", "t": "3+ years of professional interior design experience, including design and construction document production for commercial, hospitality, residential, or mixed-use projects\nBachelor’s Degree in Interior Design or Interior Architecture from a CIDA-accredited university\nAbility to commute to our Austin, TX office a minimum of three days per week\nProficiency in Revit, SketchUp, Adobe Creative Suite, and AutoCAD\nWorking knowledge of interior design practice, including design documentation, detailing, building materials, building systems, applicable building codes, and construction technologies\nStrong understanding of finishes, fixtures, furnishings, lighting, artwork, and decorative elements\nDemonstrated design ability and a strong portfolio of academic and professional work\nStrong technical skills, creative problem-solving abilities, and attention to detail\nExcellent verbal, written, and graphic communication skills\nAbility to manage multiple priorities and contribute effectively across multiple projects simultaneously\nPositive attitude, intellectual curiosity, and willingness to collaborate within a team environment"}, {"h": "Work Environment & Physical Requirements", "t": "This position is primarily performed in an office environment, with periodic travel to project sites, construction sites, client meetings, vendor showrooms, and other project-related locations.\n\nTo perform the essential functions of this position, an employee must be able to:\n\nRemain stationary and work at a computer workstation for extended periods throughout the workday\nFrequently operate a computer and other standard office equipment.\nCommunicate effectively with clients, consultants, contractors, vendors, and team members in person, by phone, and electronically\nTravel to project sites, client meetings, construction sites, and vendor locations as needed\nMove throughout active construction sites, existing buildings, project sites, and showroom environments, which may include walking, standing, climbing stairs, bending, reaching, and navigating uneven surfaces\nObserve and assess project conditions, construction progress, design details, and installed work\nOccasionally transport project materials, samples, presentation materials, or equipment weighing up to 25 pounds\nVisually review drawings, specifications, project documentation, and digital design tools for extended periods\n\nReasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of this position.\n\nTo apply to this position, please click the link below and complete the online application form.\n\nShare Job\n\nFurther project information can be found at hsuoffice.com\n\nFor any questions, please reach out to work@hsuoffice.com\n\nNo phone calls please.\n\n© 2026\nterms of use\ninfo@hsuoffice.com\n\n512.706.4303\n\ninstagram\n\nlinkedin"}], "k": ["autocad", "branding", "building-codes", "construction-administration", "construction-documents", "detailing", "finish-carpentry", "furniture-design", "presentation", "project-management", "revit", "sketchup", "social-media", "urban-design"], "r": {"exp": 3, "edu": {"level": "bachelor", "state": "required"}}}, "6a2f86ac4e": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...architects, and interior designers as part of an integrated multidisciplinary team. You will report to Interior Design leadership and use BIM platforms, including ArchiCAD or Revit, along with standard office tools and vendor resources."}], "k": ["archicad", "bim", "revit"]}, "89938d601b": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "New Search\nLogin Page\n1 of 6\nInterior Designer\nLocation\nNew York\n1. Register\nTo submit your application, please complete these steps. Fields marked with a red asterisk (*) are required.\nEmail Registration\n\nYour email address will be used as your login name allowing you to return to our website to update your profile.\n\nIf you are a returning applicant, please sign in or reset your password using the Login button.\n\nEmail\nPassword"}], "k": []}, "1c1ddab213": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Career Opportunities with EskewDumezRipple\n\nWe build places for people.\n\nCareers At EskewDumezRipple\n\nCurrent job opportunities are posted here as they become available.\n\nBack To Openings\nSenior Interior Designer\nDepartment: Design\nLocation: New Orleans, LA"}, {"h": "START YOUR APPLICATION", "t": "About EskewDumezRipple\n\nEskewDumezRipple (EDR) is a nationally recognized group of architects, designers, and thinkers operating within the fields of architecture, interior design, research, and urban strategies with studios in New Orleans and Washington DC.\n\nOur studio itself is a diverse group of people from all over the world, a resonant gathering of experiences and expertise. We are curious and determined. We nurture a culture that encourages a spirit of collaboration and attracts inquisitive people.\n\nOur work unfolds at every scale, harmoniously integrating interiors and buildings with neighborhoods and communities."}, {"h": "About the Job", "t": "We are currently seeking a Senior Interior Designer with 8+ years of experience to join our New Orleans or DC studio. This role will lead interior design efforts across a range of project types, guiding projects from early concept development through construction while supporting team leadership, technical excellence, and client engagement.\n\nRelocation assistance available."}, {"h": "Responsibilities", "t": "Lead interior design projects through all phases, from concept development through construction administration and occupancy.\nCoordinate with clients, consultants, contractors, and internal project teams to ensure alignment of project goals, design intent, schedule, budget, and technical requirements.\nDevelop and oversee high-quality design presentations, space planning studies, technical documentation, and coordinated construction document packages."}, {"h": "Ensure compliance with code and regulatory requirements.", "t": "Coordinate and integrate consultant work across multiple disciplines, including architectural, MEP, lighting, structural, acoustic, security, and hardware systems.\nDevelop FF&E, color palettes and material presentations from the conceptual phase through specifications.\nCommunicate conceptual design ideas through sketching, 3D modeling, rendering tools, and graphic storytelling methods.\nManage project workflow, schedules, deliverables, and team coordination to support successful project execution.\nProvide technical leadership and mentorship to junior designers across the studio."}, {"h": "Qualifications", "t": "Required\n\n8+ years of experience in an architecture or commercial interior design firm with a proven record of successful project completion.\nBachelor Degree in Interior Design or Architecture from an accredited institution.\nProficiency in Adobe Suite and Revit is required."}, {"h": "Preferred", "t": "Experience in Higher Education, Workplace, Hospitality, and/or Mixed-Use projects.\nLicensure as a professional interior designer or architect.\nLEED or WELL Accreditation"}, {"h": "Benefits", "t": "EskewDumezRipple offers a comprehensive benefits package including medical, dental, vision, 401K, short and long term disability, life insurance, competitive PTO, and parental leave. Our studio also hosts weekly happy hours and numerous employee events throughout the year."}, {"h": "START YOUR APPLICATION", "t": "Visit Our Home Page\n\n© 2026 EskewDumezRipple\n\nApplicant Tracking System Powered by"}], "k": ["3d-modeling", "construction-administration", "ffe", "leed", "mep", "people-management", "presentation", "recruiting", "rendering", "revit", "space-planning", "technical-writing", "writing"], "b": ["dental", "generous-pto", "life-insurance", "parental-leave", "relocation", "retirement-match", "vision"], "r": {"exp": 8, "edu": {"level": "bachelor", "state": "required"}}}, "c0d3ed304c": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "All Jobs >\nInterior Designer 4\n\nApply\nInterior Designer 4\n\nNew York, NY\n· Interior Design\nDescription"}, {"h": "Overall Responsibilities", "t": "Develop design for Public, Government, and Department of Defense projects. Bring self-motivation and strong design skills through all stages of programming, concept, design, and documentation and take initiative to drive great design. Support the firm culture of design excellence within teams as well as firmwide interior design efforts and client presentations.\n\nDesign Leadership\n\nOriginate innovative high-level design solutions to complex problems and coordinate with the larger project teams through the development and presentation of these ideas.\nWork simultaneously on multiple projects, including large, complex government facilities.\nWork closely with the Interiors Principal and Senior Staff to support internal business development efforts.\nDemonstrates a comprehensive understanding of the principles of construction documentation to assist in producing contract and proposal documents.\nPrepares and develops space plans, furniture plans, elevations, sections, interiors details, FF&E cost estimates, FF&E schedules, SID binders, FF&E binders, technical specifications, best value determination (BVD) documentation, 3D conceptual views and finished design presentation documentation for all design phases of a project in accordance with specifications and project schedule.\nAttends project team meetings and department staff meetings and oversees the development and distribution of meeting minutes.\nOperate with a service-focused mindset with external clients and colleagues. Dedicated to meeting client requirements, expectations, and budget.\nWork closely with the Project Architects and Senior Staff to ensure that construction documents are consistent with design intent and meet the firm’s BIM standards.\nCommitment to advance the firm’s stance in the use of ethical and highly sustainable materials."}, {"h": "Leadership Responsibilities", "t": "General familiarity of project finances and appropriate balancing of scope, project tasks, and fee, including assistance in the staffing of each project.\nMentor junior interior design staff to support their development and growth.\nContinually seek self-growth in firm practice areas.\nContinually seek self-growth in firm practice areas. Stay abreast of trends and development in the areas of specific project types.\nActive participation in firmwide initiatives, external professional organizations, and industry social functions."}, {"h": "Requirements", "t": "Six (6) years of experience in the design and documentation of interiors projects\nBachelor's Degree in Interior Design or Architecture\nNCIDQ Certification with strong grasp of ADA and life safety requirements"}, {"h": "LEED or WELL accreditation preferred", "t": "Experience in interior design, documentation and detailing on every phase of a project\nExperience with public sector projects including state & local government facilities and Department of Defense work preferred\nKnowledge of highly sustainable practices and industry standards\nExcellent graphic, verbal, and written communication skills, as well as excellent organizational and time management skills\nKnowledge of FF&E, color, and materials\nKnowledge of furniture systems and specifications\nKnowledge of a design-build process a plus\nProficiency in relevant computer software\nBuilding Information Modeling: Revit; including firm grasp of collaborative tools such as R360\nAdobe Creative Suite: InDesign, Photoshop, Illustrator\nAdobe Acrobat or Bluebeam\nMicrosoft Office Suite\nKnowledge of Enscape and AutoCAD a plus"}, {"h": "Pay/Benefits", "t": "We offer a competitive salary and benefits package that includes medical, dental, vision, life, short- and long-term disability, paid PTO and holidays, as well as 401(k) matching, profit sharing and annual performance bonus opportunities.\n\nSteinberg Hart is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, or protected veteran status and will not be discriminated against on the basis of disability, genetics, or arrest/conviction records.\n\nApply\nView All Jobs\nPowered by\nPrivacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software\n\nBy clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts.\n\nCookies Settings Accept All Cookies"}], "k": ["autocad", "bim", "bluebeam", "business-development", "construction-documents", "detailing", "enscape", "ffe", "indesign", "leed", "photoshop", "presentation", "revit", "scheduling"], "b": ["bonus", "generous-pto", "retirement-match"]}, "846bfc35ac": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Skip to content\nHomepage\nSenior Interior Designer - Shanghai\nOn-site\nShanghai, Shanghai Shi, China\nShanghai\nJob details\nApply\nJob description\n\nAs an international architectural firm, UNS is active in the broadest fields of architecture. Our project portfolio covers every aspect of architecture, ranging from small to large scale projects, research and theory.\n\nThe atmosphere within our global offices, including our UNS Asia offices in Shanghai and Hong Kong, is international, multidisciplinary, design-oriented and ambitious, but also open, non-hierarchical, team-based and friendly, with attention to personal well-being, knowledge development, and career planning.\n\nUNS is currently looking for Senior Interior Designers to immediately join our Shanghai office."}, {"h": "Requirement & Skills", "t": "· Master’s or professional degree in interior design, architecture or related disciplines\n\n· 8-10 years of experience as an Interior Designer or Architect with equivalent interior design experience.\n\n· Extensive experience in cultural, large-scale retail, commercial, hospitality & mixed-use projects\n\n· Excellent technical interfacing and detailing skills, with the ability to develop innovative interior design solutions (documented through construction documents or shop drawing packages)\n\n· Experience in writing performance specifications\n\n· Enthusiasm for and extensive knowledge of both standard and customized materials and finishes\n\n· Strong aesthetic sensibilities and design skills, with the ability to develop and implement a design concept from preliminary 3D studies through to construction documentation and detailing\n\n· Proactive and self-motivated, with a commitment to advancing design\n\n· Good team player with the ability to organize both own work and others, clearly communicate with Project Leaders, and coach/motivate team members\n\n· Fluent English communication skills; additional fluency in Mandarin and/or Cantonese is a plus\n\n· Enthusiasm for and knowledge of interior products, materials, and finishes\n\n· 3D Modeling experience in Rhinoceros is required (3D visualization abilities are preferred)\n\n· Expert knowledge of AutoCAD and Adobe Creative Suite (InDesign, Illustrator, Photoshop)\n\nContact\nWorking conditions are according to local legislation. Benefits follow UNS Shanghai standards. Applications consisting of a short cover letter, CV, portfolio (PDF, max.10mb enclosed in the application email or Issuu.com only), last & expected salary and availability can be sent digitally to hr.asia@unstudio.com."}, {"h": "When you work at UNS", "t": "· you have the opportunity to work on high profile, challenging global projects\n\n· you are part of a creative, fresh, professional and academic working environment\n\n· your experience is highly valued, but your innovative and entrepreneurial attitude is prized highest\n\n· you work in an international team that is highly ambitious, collegial and self-motivated, made up of recently-graduated architects, experienced senior architects, and every level in-between\n\n· you design through knowledge and discovery, and continually learn on the job\n\nApply\n\nor\n\nApply with Indeed\nShare job"}], "k": ["3d-modeling", "autocad", "construction-documents", "detailing", "indesign", "photoshop", "rhino"], "r": {"exp": 8, "edu": {"level": "master", "state": "required"}, "lang": ["English", "Mandarin"]}}, "b1b58d9f90": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...sensibility with the ability to make thoughtful, aesthetic decisions\nFluency in English is mandatory\nExperience in the U.S. market will be valued\nEffective communicator with initiative and ability to understand drawings deeply\nAvailable to work..."}], "k": ["revit"]}, "729fd642a3": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...junior designers, and driving a cohesive, design-forward narrative across disciplines.\nYou will collaborate with architects, planners, BIM integration leaders, and urban designers to deliver integrated, evidence-based spaces that heal and engage users.\n#J-18808-Ljbffr..."}], "k": ["bim"]}, "de3514a1b3": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...renderings, and coordinating interior design with the integrated design team to meet scope, schedule, budget, and fees.\nYou will lead interior design efforts, interact with clients, and present concepts while applying BIM standards and QA/QC processes.\n#J-18808-Ljbffr..."}], "k": ["bim", "quality-control"]}, "ec91636f87": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...American Society of Interior Designers is seeking an Interior Designer