creative skills. Candidates should be bilingual in English and..."}], "k": ["autocad", "translation"]}, "926fcf58c0": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...AvroKO Designer Position\nJoin our San Francisco office and be a part of a global network of offices spanning five cities (New York,... ...experience with significant experience in high-end, conceptually driven interior design\nDemonstrated conceptual approach to design..."}], "k": []}, "be6b219187": {"s": [{"h": "...Job Summary", "t": "Supports senior design staff in developing technical drawings and documentation for VA facility projects."}, {"h": "Qualifications", "t": "~ Degree in Interior Design or related field\n~1–3 years experience\n~ Working..."}], "k": ["cad-drafting", "construction-documents"]}, "7a238c829f": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...Junior Interior Designer\nOvadia Interior Design and Architecture is a nationally recognized interior design and architecture studio in the heart of Manhattan, known for blending modern elegance, warmth, and a little bit of magic into every space we create. We design..."}], "k": []}, "ec074e560e": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...Job Title: Jr. Interior Designer for Hospitality Design Firm"}, {"h": "What We Do", "t": "For almost 40 years, EDG Interior Architecture + Design has shaped hospitality experiences around the world through branding, interior design, and strategies storytelling. With offices in the San..."}], "k": ["branding", "writing"]}, "0673903b97": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...Ovadia Design Group is looking for a Junior Interior Designer based in Manhattan, New York. This entry-level position requires detail-oriented design skills and proficiency in AutoCAD and Studio Designer. The role involves developing design presentations and producing..."}], "k": ["autocad", "presentation"]}, "d3bf1a5836": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...Oakline Studio is looking for a professional, organized and self-motivated Junior Interior Designer who has 1-5 years minimum of design experience and who can thrive in an intimate, but very fast-growing firm. Candidate must be good at multi-tasking, organized, energetic..."}], "k": [], "r": {"exp": 1}}, "b76b29282a": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...Louisiana\nFull-Time | In-Office\nSiS is a commercial furniture and interiors partner delivering turnkey solutions for healthcare, corporate... ...Coast and beyond.\nWe are seeking a Junior Commercial Interior Designer to join our growing design team. This is an entry-level..."}], "k": []}, "d08f6216c2": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "... Designer / Architectural Drafter\nAs a Designer, your role is to aid in producing presentation and construction documents and help maintain... ...and Designers to support our clients. Main Line Design is the interior design arm of the company. Our main objective is to provide a..."}], "k": ["construction-documents"]}, "8975de88bd": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...Neal Beckstedt Studio in Manhattan is seeking a junior architectural designer to lead renderings for all projects and assist on residential work from start to finish. The role includes spearheading design presentations and creating renderings in SketchUp, 3Dmax, and Photoshop..."}], "k": ["photoshop", "presentation", "sketchup"]}, "8dd3f1e242": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Innenarchitekt /Einrichtungs\\-Berater als RETAIL\\-MANAGER \"Sales Store \\& Service\" (w/m)\nPremium\\-Konsumgüter im Fokus Ihrer neuen, Herausforderung!\n\nModerne Designs, innovative Kreationen und eine überzeugende Marktstellung zeichnen die qualitäts\\- und trendmässig einzigartigen Produkte und Dienstleistungen meines Kunden, ein national bestens bekanntes und lokal verankertes Unternehmen mit Pionierstatus im Segment von hochwertigen und langlebigen Konsumgütern aus dem Büro\\- und Wohnbereich mit grossem Showroom in Zürich\\-City aus.\n\nIch bin mit der Suche beauftragt nach einer verkaufs\\- und beratungsstarken Persönlichkeit mit Drive und Enthusiasmus (machen Sie aus Ihrem Beruf eine Leidenschaft . . .)\nInnenarchitekt /Einrichtungs\\-Berater als RETAIL\\-MANAGER \"Sales Store \\& Service\" (w/m)"}, {"h": "Ihre Aufgaben", "t": "Hauptverantwortung über den gesamten Retail\\-Bereich des Unternehmens, von der Umsatz\\- und Deckungsbeitragsverantwortung über die strategisch\\-konzeptionellen Aufgaben bis hin zu Change\\-Projekten in Bezug auf Marktveränderungen und Digitalisierung\nAus\\- und Aufbau von bestehenden respektive neuen Geschäftsfeldern; Akquisition und Betreuung von Projekten im Bereich Gesamteinrichtungen und Planungen\nPersonelle und fachliche Führung der Retail\\- und Verkauf\\-Innendienst\\-Teams bestehend aus Sales\\-, und Beratungs\\- und Sachbearbeitungs\\-Spezialisten sowie gezielte Weiterentwicklung der Mitarbeitenden hinsichtlich Fachwissen, Aussenwirkung und Methodenkompetenz\nAktive Mitwirkung im Shop\\-Business wie auch persönliche Betreuung von Architekten, Beeinflussern sowie Lieferanten und Produzenten\nEnge Zusammenarbeit mit der Inhaberschaft, Mitarbeit bei interdisziplinären Spezialprojekten im gesamten Unternehmen (Marketing, Kollektions\\-Entwicklungen etc.), Organisation und Teilnahme von Ausstellungen, Messen und Events"}, {"h": "Ihr Profil", "t": "Grundausbildung im Bereich Architektur, Möbel, Einrichtungen oder vergleichbarem Know\\-how plus Weiterentwicklung in Richtung Management, Betriebswirtschaft, Verkauf und/oder RetailNachhaltiger\nLeistungsausweis in einer operativen Gesamttätigkeit bezüglich Verkauf und Planung im Umfeld von Inneneinrichtungen, Wohnen und Accessoires\nMehrere Jahre Führungs\\-Erfahrung in einem Unternehmen mit flacher Hierarchie im lokalen respektive nationalen Retail\\-Markt\nPerfektes Deutsch in Wort und Schrift, gutes Business\\-Englisch, weitere Sprachkenntnisse von Vorteil, wohnhaft und vernetzt in der Region Zürich\nGute Computer\\-Kenntnisse (Microsoft\\-Palette, ERP\\-System), Organisationstalent, sicheres und dynamisches Auftreten, begeisterungsfähig und lösungsorientiert, Persönlichkeit mit \"sportlicher Einstellung\"\nKann ich Sie begeistern, in einem namhaften, und erfolgreichen schweizerischen KMU mit Charakter eine entscheidende Rolle einzunehmen? Sind Sie motiviert, komplexe und anspruchsvolle Aufgaben anzugehen und dabei einen effektiven Mehrwert für Ihr berufliches Umfeld zu erzielen?\n\nSenden Sie doch bitte Ihre vollständige Bewerbung mit Foto per E\\-Mail an Henchoz, ich stehe Ihnen auch für zusätzliche, telefonische Auskünfte zur Verfügung und freue mich, Sie kennen zu lernen! jpidd06afbcjm jit0834jm jiy26jm"}], "k": ["brewing", "sap"], "r": {"lang": ["English"]}}, "19b15eccac": {"s": [{"h": "CURRENT POSITIONS", "t": "We are currently accepting applications for the following positions. To be considered, please send your resume, work samples or portfolio, and a cover letter to employment@shapelessstudio.com with the relevant job title in the subject line. Please keep any attachments to under 8MB. Applications without cover letter will not be considered. You will receive a response by e-mail if we would like to schedule an interview."}, {"h": "Engaging with clients to learn requirements, tastes, priorities", "t": "Preparing client presentations of furniture layouts, selections, finishes, budgets\nSourcing and ordering FF&E\nDeveloping technical drawing packages and specification schedules"}, {"h": "QUALIFICATIONS", "t": "Degree in Interior Design or related field\nProficiency in AutoCAD (drafting) and Rhino and/or Sketchup (modeling)\nStrong communication, organization, problem solving, critical thinking skills\n3+ years of professional experience"}, {"h": "Has enthusiasm for taking on new challenges and responsibilities", "t": "Is a quick and intuitive learner, resourceful and able to work independently\nHas an interest in learning about all aspects of design and project management\nEnjoys collaborating as a team and is excited to share new ideas"}, {"h": "SHAPELESS STUDIO ARCHITECTURE & INTERIORS", "t": "492 Atlantic Avenue,\nBrooklyn, NY, 11217,\nUnited States\n(347)799-1199\nhello@shapelessstudio.com"}], "k": ["autocad", "ffe", "presentation", "procurement", "project-management", "rhino", "sketchup"]}, "85df6b982d": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "People First.\nHistory Culture Team Careers\nDesign Forward.\nProcess Sustainability News\nWork\nCivic Commercial Community Education Healthcare Hospitality Houses Interiors Multi-Family On the Boards\nContact\nHealthcare Interior Designer or Interior Architect\n\nScott Edwards Architecture is seeking a Healthcare Interior Designer or Interior Architect to join our Health and Wellness studio.\n\nThe Health and Wellness studio designs the full spectrum of outpatient and inpatient environments. Projects range widely in both scale and type and include both new construction and tenant improvements. For this role we are seeking a self-directed, collaborative, client-focused candidate to design, document, and administer highly functional, durable, and inspirational spaces.\n\nScott Edwards Architecture is a firm built on the idea that innovative design solutions result from a collaborative effort between designer, client, and community. We lead our clients on an exploration of possibilities, guided by traditional principles of design, clarified through a contemporary perspective.\n\nTo this end we look for talented, versatile team members who enjoy working in an open studio environment that facilitates interaction and creativity. Our working environment is defined by enthusiasm, collaboration, and support. As a firm, our commitment extends well beyond specific projects.\n\nWe forge lasting relationships with clients and actively support organizations that similarly embrace our pursuit of social, cultural, and environmental sustainability.\n\nThis studio is passionate about the work they do, and it shows in the care taken with and precision of resulting designs.\n\nHealth and wellness serve a vital role in our communities and SEA takes great pride in our contributions to these places—from community health centers to hospital expansions, we have had a hand in many exciting and impactful designs.\n\nCandidates who are considering applying for the role of Healthcare Interior Designer or Interior Architect can expect to be part of complex and meaningful work.\n\nOnly resumes supporting the following qualifications and experience will be considered:\n\nInterior Design, Interior Architecture or Architectural degree from an accredited school\n\n10+ years professional experience in design and construction document production with healthcare projects\n\nHigh proficiency in interior detailing required\n\nStrong technical and design skills in the production of construction documents with a commitment to high quality design\n\nExposure to projects pursuing state required licensure\n\nFamiliarity with ADA, OARs, NFPA & FGI for Healthcare\n\nAbility to build and maintain positive relationships with clients and consultants, while being mindful of project budgets and schedules\n\nProficiency in creating quality spaces that meet client design standards\n\nStrong written and verbal communication skills. Experience with client presentations.\n\nProficiency in Revit is required with skill in Adobe Creative Suite and SketchUp preferred\n\nConstruction Administration experience including attending regular site meetings, RFI responses, submittal and shop drawing reviews\n\nWELL and/or LEED certification a plus\n\nAbility to mentor junior designers in healthcare design a plus\n\nCandidates with more extensive healthcare experience will be compensated accordingly.\n\nPlease submit a cover letter, resume and sampling of your work for immediate consideration at careers@seallp.com. No phone calls please. We are an equal opportunity employer and recognize the value of a diverse workforce, therefore all qualified individuals will be considered for employment.\n\nScott Edwards Architecture offers a competitive salary and benefit package. Our ‘People First. Design Forward.’ philosophy has resulted in SEA being named one of Oregon’s “100 Best Companies to Work For” by both Oregon Business Magazine and The Oregonian. Learn more about the culture here at SEA.\n\n503-226-3617\n\nhello@seallp.com\n\n2525 E. Burnside St.\nPortland, OR 97214\n\n© 2022 Scott Edwards Architecture, LLP.\n\nKeep up with us\n\nSign me up"}], "k": ["construction-administration", "construction-documents", "detailing", "health-education", "leed", "presentation", "revit", "sketchup", "sustainability"], "r": {"exp": 10}}, "cd6977e6a5": {"s": [{"h": "The Role", "t": "We’re seeking a Senior Interior Designer with proven experience leading workplace design projects. This is a chance to take ownership of high profile projects, work directly with clients and mentor the next generation of designers. You’ll be central to shaping environments that inspire people and ideas to thrive."}, {"h": "Key Responsibilities", "t": "Lead the design and delivery of workplace projects from concept to completion\nManage client relationships and present design concepts with confidence\nCollaborate with architects, engineers and consultants for seamless project execution\nMentor and guide junior and mid level designers\nOversee project timelines, budgets and deliverables\nPrepare design documentation, specifications and presentations"}, {"h": "What We’re Looking For", "t": "6–7+ years’ experience in workplace design, including 1–2+ years in a senior or project lead role\nStrong portfolio demonstrating workplace design excellence for high calibre clients\nProficiency in Revit, AutoCAD, Enscape and Adobe Creative Suite\nExcellent communication, presentation and leadership skills\nA collaborative, detail driven approach with the ability to manage multiple projects"}, {"h": "What We Offer", "t": "The opportunity to lead projects for world class clients\nInternational exposure through projects across Europe\nA clear path for career progression and leadership\nA hybrid work model (2–3 days in our new Dublin studio)\nA collaborative, supportive and award winning team culture\n\nTo apply for any of the above roles, please send your CV and portfolio with a short cover note and make sure to include the position you are applying for in the subject line to paul@mola.ie by 5th September 2025.\n\nInterviews will take place in our Dublin Studio during the last two weeks of September."}, {"h": "POPULAR POSTS", "t": "Five Promotions Mark Continued Growth at MOLA\nFriday - May 22, 2026\nArchitectural Technologist\nSunday - May 10, 2026\nMOLA Architecture Opens a New Office in Limerick\nFriday - February 27, 2026\nSenior Interior Designer\nWednesday - August 27, 2025\nMOLA Architecture Leads Design Team for Land Development Agency to…\nWednesday - August 20, 2025\nMOLA Architecture Moves Up – A New Home for a…\nFriday - March 28, 2025\nRIAI Architecture Ireland 2024\nFriday - February 28, 2025\nTully Park Cherrywood has been awarded Overall Winner in the…\nThursday - January 02, 2025\nPinterest Wins Project of the Year UK & Ireland Workplace…\nWednesday - December 18, 2024\nMOLA Wins 5 Awards at the Fit Out Awards 2024\nFriday - December 06, 2024"}], "k": ["account-management", "autocad", "enscape", "presentation", "revit"], "r": {"exp": 6}}, "4703a35d1a": {"s": [{"h": "/VACANCIES", "t": "Omega Architects B.V. is a medium-sized internationally operating design office in the field of architecture, yachtdesign and interior design. We offer a multidisciplinary working environment that inspires growth and deepening.\n\nEXTERIOR / INTERIOR DESIGNER M/F (1fte)\n\nTasks & Offer\nBeing an exterior / interior designer at Omega Architects, you assist our senior designers to develop exterior and interior designs in 3D. You will assist in the total spiral of design, consisting of 3 different design stages. Our scope of supply has to be matched constantly with the principals set of requirements.\nYou will assist in the conceptual (first) design stage and tailor our standard scope of supply to the specific requirements of each specific design commission for the following 2 stages.\nTherefore, among your responsibilities is our communication with principals and third parties.\nYour responsibility as a team member also requires updating your project presentations, for both internal use as well as for our principals. You will update the particular data of the project.\nYou will research design trends and keep track of publications about yacht design. In many cases, your research will be tailored to our design commissions, in order to advise the senior yacht designer. You will define and update a plan of training and education in order to improve your skills, amongst the available skills of the team."}, {"h": "Required qualifications", "t": "· Applicable education like a Bachelor or Master’s degree in yacht design, interior design or naval architecture.\n· A background in a yacht design agency or ship building industry.\n· The ambition to optimize the expertise of our exterior design team.\n· Good 3D hand sketching skills\n· Good communicative skills in English (Dutch is a plus), both written and spoken.\n· Living in -or willing to relocate to Netherlands.\n· Valid EU work permit required\n\nSkills\n· 3D visualization, Rhinoceros and 3DSMax.\n· AutoCAD\n· Photoshop and other Adobe applications.\n\nOur offer\n· A fulltime (40 hrs) job in our team;\n· A salary depending on your education and experience, paid according to the Collective Employment Agreement (CAO) for Architectural firms and APA system.\n\nContact\nPlease send your CV and portfolio to omega@omega-architects.com attn. Mrs. L. de Groot.\nWe will respond to your application only if you meet the requirements and provide your info as requested.\nNo free-lancers, no acquisition."}, {"h": "OMEGA ARCHITECTS", "t": "Klepperheide 22\n6651 KM Druten\nThe Netherlands\n\nTel. +31 487 51 8889\nomega@omega-architects.com"}, {"h": "BACK TO TOP", "t": "Privacy Policy\nVacancies\nCopyright © 2026 Omega Architects"}], "k": ["3ds-max", "autocad", "photoshop", "presentation", "research", "rhino"], "r": {"edu": {"level": "bachelor", "state": "required"}}}, "6e5d5f78e7": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Latinolegends, a fast-growing U.S.-based interior design firm, seeks a Virtual Interior Designer to craft high-end"}], "k": []}, "a267eba3e6": {"s": [{"h": "Who You Are", "t": "You are passionate about the impact of design on people’s lives and thrive on developing architectural solutions to complex... ...Experience and Skillset\nBachelor’s degree in Architecture or Interior Design.\n10+ years of work experience in an architectural or..."}], "k": [], "r": {"exp": 10, "edu": {"level": "bachelor", "state": "required"}}}, "81d76a5f73": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...for new processes, technologies, and techniques to increase efficiencies and scalability to improve our services.\nThe Junior Interior Designer supports the planning and design of innovative workplace markets and food service environments that enhance the customer experience..."}], "k": []}, "b74539a1e1": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...woodworking studio on the North Shore of Long Island, Allied Maker has grown into a design studio with a strong manufacturing backbone."}, {"h": "The Role", "t": "Allied Maker is seeking a Junior Interior Designer to support the development of our new headquarters, showrooms, and other..."}], "k": []}, "ae9323635f": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "... Interior Designer - Junior\nAre you an emerging designer with a sharp eye, curiosity, and drive to learn? At Mancini, Junior Interior Designers are trusted team players who help bring bold ideas to life. You'll gain hands-on experience across all phases of design while..."}], "k": []}, "9365867597": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Job Title"}, {"h": "A Taste of Who We Are", "t": "Backed by a tireless commitment to high quality, innovative culinary offerings and unparalleled client and guest services, Continental consistently ranks among the top contract dining and refreshment providers in the nation according..."}], "k": ["food-service", "guest-relations"]}, "6aa1ae7dd9": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...Description: To mainly assist the work load of the Designer and/or Senior Designer on client projects to help ensure a smooth operation of job description mentioned below, while playing a critical role in production.\nDesign\nProduce drawings and presentation documents..."}], "k": []}, "0f1158a6ec": {"s": [{"h": "...About the Role", "t": "The Junior Interior Designer (Intern) supports the day‑to‑day delivery of interior design tasks across real estate developments under the close supervision of the Interior Designer and Senior Interior Designer. The role focuses on Autodesk Revit modelling..."}], "k": ["revit"]}, "2e6f7c6612": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...Pembrooke and Ives is looking for a Junior Interior Architect with at least 2 years' experience to work closely with Designers, Project Managers, and Studio Directors to provide support and co-ordination throughout the project delivery process as a member of the Design..."}], "k": ["project-management"], "r": {"exp": 2}}, "0393400027": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "If you think your skills, experience and aspirations make you a good match for this position, we encourage you to apply. This position may be filled in the Chicago, IL office."}, {"h": "ABOUT THE ROLE", "t": "This position will have a design or technical focus and be a member of our multi-disciplinary team, collaborating with design and technical leadership and will be an integral part of project teams. Your initial assignment will be on a 2.0+ million square foot healthcare facility at Mayo Clinic’s campus. Under the direct supervision of designated project leadership, the primary responsibilities will include the following:"}, {"h": "HERE'S WHAT YOU'LL DO", "t": "With limited direction, Assist Senior Interior Designer and/or Project Manager with the execution of the project goals throughout all phases (Programming, Schematic Design, Design Development, Construction Documents, and Construction Administration).\nAssist in the development of the design including planning and three-dimensional studies.\nIndependently assist in the design development and documentation of interior spaces to include drawings of floor plans, reflected ceiling plans, pattern designs, elevations, details, etc.\nProvide support to the Senior Interior Designer with furniture, fixtures and equipment (FFE) selection, layout and specifications throughout all phases of interior design work, as required.\nProduce drawings in conformance with project time, cost and quality constraints.\nIdentify, research and apply building and life safety codes to applicable interior design work.\nPrepare renderings and other presentation materials.\nFollow CannonDesign drawing standards.\nParticipate in client meetings with Senior Interior Designer to gain client interaction and presentation experience.\nParticipate in construction administration activities, including site visits, review of submittals and shop drawings, and conducting punch list. Site visits frequently require a physical walk-through of site.\nMentor less experienced interior design staff and provide guidance in the development of project documents.\nActively participate and promote design quality.\nUnderstand proper application of materials."}, {"h": "HERE'S WHAT YOU'LL NEED", "t": "Bachelor or Master's degree in Interior Design, Interior Architecture, or relevant field required."}, {"h": "Current NCIDQ certification is preferred.", "t": "Must be able to participate the development of projects' technical or design characteristics and content.\nStrong creative design portfolio is essential as are strong communication, teamwork, presentation, graphics, organizational skills and the ability to handle multiple projects.\nProficiency with Revit, Enscape, Bluebeam, Microsoft Office, and Adobe Creative Suite required.\nProfessional business attire is required for all client meetings. Examples of professional business attire include suits, ties, collared dress shirts, dresses, and skirts.\nTravel required.\nThe salary range for this position to be filled in the Chicago, IL office is $57,905 to $72,335 annually. This salary range is the range we believe is the anticipated range of possible base compensation at the timing of the posting. We may ultimately pay more or less than the anticipated salary range for the position.\n\nEmployees may be eligible for discretionary bonuses. We offer a full benefit package including medical, dental and vision coverage and flexible spending account options and voluntary insurances. We have paid time off, flex-time schedules, remote work options and a 401k plan and employee perk programs.\n\nFor a general overview of our benefits, please visit our careers page at https://www.cannondesign.com/careers/benefits . Actual compensation may vary from posting based on geographic location, work experience, education and/or skill level."}, {"h": "ABOUT OUR FIRM", "t": "CannonDesign is a design practice where strategy, experience, architecture, engineering, and social impact converge. We don’t just dream up solutions — we create and bring them to life in ways to solve some of the biggest challenges facing our clients and the society.\n\nAt the heart of everything we do is Living-Centered Design, a bold commitment to using our talents to not just improve the world but to truly reshape it for the better. It’s more than a philosophy — it’s who we are, and it drives us to make a meaningful, lasting difference every day."}, {"h": "ABOUT WORKING HERE", "t": "We are relentless in our pursuit of client adoration (not simply satisfaction). Consistent delivery of the best service is what we are about.\nWe are committed to ensuring our practice provides equal opportunities for all employees, as we strive to connect with communities around us and focus on the future of design. We support equity, diversity, and inclusion efforts that benefit all employees through the leadership of our DEI Council, our Employee Resource Groups which are open to everyone, and other community initiatives.\nWe’re about communication and transparency here. If you want to talk to someone about an idea you have, or a challenge that needs addressing, we’re ready for you.\nPlease note that candidates can only apply to our positions on our company Careers site. It's not uncommon for scammers to create positions that look legitimate on other sites; never enter your information or apply for CannonDesign positions on any platform. Should an issue arise that you feel we should be aware of, please contact us. Please provide your resume and portfolio when applying.\nAs a condition of employment, all employees are expected to complete mandatory training, including compliance training, within required timeframes and adhere to our internal policies and our Code of Conduct.\nCannonDesign is an Equal Opportunity Employer. CannonDesign is committed to maintaining a work environment that is free from any and all forms of unlawful discrimination and harassment.\n\nIt is therefore the firm’s policy to prohibit discrimination and harassment against any applicant, CannonDesign employee, vendor, contractor, or client on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, pregnancy, veteran status, genetic information, citizenship status, or any other basis prohibited by applicable law.\n\nIt is also CannonDesign’s policy to prohibit any and all forms of retaliation against any individual who has complained of harassing or discriminatory conduct, or participated in a firm or agency investigation into such complaints."}], "k": ["bluebeam", "cad-drafting", "construction-administration", "construction-documents", "enscape", "ffe", "revit"], "b": ["generous-pto", "vision"], "r": {"exp": 4, "edu": {"level": "bachelor", "state": "required"}}}, "a4a727ed79": {"s": [{"h": null, "t