ctive/Denton House... ...Do:\nWe are seeking a creative and detail-oriented Junior Interior Designer to support our design team in delivering exceptional design..."}], "k": []}, "59ff32eaf4": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Oversee section operations which include planning workload, assigning projects, employee training and development, position management, performance evaluation, grievance resolution, and EEO compliance.\nUtilize Building Information Modeling/ Computer-Aided Design drawing systems to develop in-house designs for architectural, Structural/Comprehensive (SID/CID) specifications, and furniture, fixtures, or other equipment packages.\nDirect technical reviews, construction phase support, and submittal evaluations (shop drawings, materials, samples), to resolve complex on-site architectural and interior design deficiencies.\nProvide technical advisory and program oversight, including Center of Standardization (COS) initiatives, facility condition assessments, and cross-discipline engineering coordination for military construction and civil works projects.\nDirect in-house architectural and interior design development, client consultations, Building information Modeling (BIM), construction document preparation, and post-bidding construction support and submittal reviews.\nWho May Apply: Only applicants who meet one of the employment authority categories below are eligible to apply for this job. You will be asked to identify which category or categories you meet, and to provide documents which prove you meet the category or categories you selected.\n\nSee Proof of Eligibility for an extensive list of document requirements for all employment authorities.\n\nCurrent Department of Army Civilian Employees Domestic Defense Industrial Base/Major Range and Test Facilities Base Civilian Personnel Workforce Interagency Career Transition Assistance Plan Land Management Workforce Flexibility Act Military Spouses, under Executive Order (E.O.) 13473 Priority Placement Program, DoD Military Reserve (MR) and National Guard (NG) Technician Eligible Priority Placement Program, DoD Military Spouse Preference (MSP) Eligible Priority Placement Program, DoD MR and NG Preference Eligible Tech Receiving Disability Retirement Priority Placement Program, DoD Retained Grade Preference Eligible Veterans Employment Opportunity Act (VEOA) of 1998 In order to qualify, you must meet the experience requirements described below.\n\nExperience refers to paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., Peace Corps, AmeriCorps) and other organizations (e.g., professional; philanthropic; religious; spiritual; community; student; social). You will receive credit for all qualifying experience, including volunteer experience.\n\nYour resume must clearly describe your relevant experience; if qualifying based on education, your transcripts will be required as part of your application. Additional information about transcripts is in this document. This position has selective placement factor which must be met prior to employment and for continued employment.\n\nSelective Placement Factor: This position has a requirement for certification under the National Council for Interior Design Qualification (NCIDQ) .\n\n(Please upload proof of certificate with your application package.) Specialized Experience: One year of specialized experience which includes 1.) Developing architectural designs, Structural/Comprehensive Interior Design (SID/CID) specifications, and Building Information Modeling (BIM)/CADD drawings for facility renovations and new construction; 2.) Reviewing and evaluating Architect-Engineer (A-E) plans, specifications, submittals, and shop drawings to ensure compliance with building codes and Unified Facilities Criteria; 3.) Conducting on-site facility investigations, condition assessments, and construction evaluations to resolve architectural, interior finish, and life safety deficiencies; and 4.) Providing technical advisory services, coordinating multidisciplinary engineering requirements, and evaluating building materials, finishes, and furniture, fixtures, or other equipment (FF&E) requirements.\n\nThis definition of specialized experience is typical of work performed at the next lower grade/level position in the federal service (GS-12). Some federal jobs allow you to substitute your education for the required experience in order to qualify.\n\nFor this job, you must meet the qualification requirement using experience alone--no substitution of education for experience is permitted. Time in Grade Requirement: Applicants who have held a General Schedule (GS) position within the last 52 weeks must have 52 weeks of Federal service at the next lower grade or equivalent (GS-12)."}], "k": ["bim", "building-codes", "cad-drafting", "construction-administration", "criminal-investigation", "ffe", "training"], "r": {"exp": 1}}, "20d309b42b": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "consultants, driving BIM and Revit workflows, and ensuring code compliance and constructability. The position offers the... translated into buildable solutions. Manage BIM and Revit documentation for interior architecture projects, establishing"}], "k": ["bim", "building-codes", "revit"]}, "17d1c827a1": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Bold Business is seeking a design-driven Interior Designer in Ciudad Autónoma de Buenos Aires to join a top-tier"}], "k": []}, "5a2d4b0aa6": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Interior Designer - Technical/Documentation Focused - Hospitality Interior Design Projects Las Vegas, NV **Relocation... precision. We're seeking a Technical Interior Designer who can transform high-level creative vision into fully coordinated"}], "k": ["technical-writing"]}, "746746a66c": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Interior Designer (Career Progression) £32,000 - £45,000 + Exciting Career Progression + Further technical training"}], "k": []}, "a969fb89d8": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...What to Expect As ajuniorinterior designer in 