{"h": null, "t": "...Suite 530, Austin, TX 78701\nWork Location\nAustin and San Antonio\nDescription\nStudio8 Architects is a full-service architecture and interior design firm founded in Austin in 2003 and San Antonio in 2011. We are a community of creatives, strategists and thinkers solving..."}], "k": []}, "98c98465c9": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...Description Delawie, A LEO A DALY studio, is seeking an experienced and talented Interior Designer to join our team. The successful candidate will contribute to inspirational design within an existing interior design group. The successful candidate filling this position..."}], "k": []}, "03f7c77ad2": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...Federal service that has given me the particular knowledge, skills and abilities required to successfully perform the duties of an Interior Designer, and that is typically in or related to the work of the position to be filled. Specialized experience is experience that..."}], "k": []}, "bc6950e4c7": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...VMDO Architects is seeking a creative problem-solver to join our Charlottesville office as a Junior Interior Designer. This position will work under the direct supervision of an experienced Lead Interior Designer and is ideal for someone with strong interpersonal skills..."}], "k": []}, "0a998e1caf": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...MAWD | March and White Design create interiors for the world’s most celebrated brands, developers and ambitious personal projects. Established in 2010, MAWD is an award-winning interior design firm with studios in London, New York, Los Angeles and Dubai. Our portfolio..."}], "k": []}, "cc3508b556": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "...Chillicothe VA Medical Center. The position is in the Planning & Design Department, Facilities Management Service (FMS) and works under... ...Project Engineer Supervisor. Incumbent assists with the interior design of the medical center, consisting of approximately 70 buildings..."}], "k": ["facilities-operations"]}, "28dfad77fa": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "... Interior Designer"}, {"h": "Primary Duties include, but not limited to", "t": "Consults, advises, plans and designs all spaces in new and or renovated construction areas.\nDevelops and directs planning and scheduling of short and long-range interior improvement projects for..."}], "k": ["scheduling"]}, "2897bfbab2": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "... Interior Designer II\nAre you ready to grow your interior design career while shaping environments that matter? At SMRT, interior design is an integral part of how we solve complex problems through the built environment. As an Interior Designer II, you'll contribute..."}], "k": []}, "eaa9aa2715": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "If you think your skills, experience and aspirations make you a good match for this position, we encourage you to apply. This position may be filled anywhere in the United States."}, {"h": "ABOUT THE ROLE", "t": "This senior-level position is a leadership role within our multi-disciplinary team, responsible for guiding and mentoring project teams across multiple interior design projects. The Interior Designer V will demonstrate expertise in furniture planning, specification, procurement coordination, design leadership, storytelling, and strategic impact.\n\nThis role requires proactive communication, independent conceptualization, and a commitment to quality and standards. The individual will serve as a furniture subject matter expert, collaborate with design leaders and contribute to business development and community engagement."}, {"h": "HERE'S WHAT YOU'LL DO", "t": "Provide leadership to the client and project team in establishment of the project goals and vision.\nOperates with high autonomy and strategic influence, guiding firm-wide standards, mentoring teams, and setting design direction independently.\nProvide interior design leadership across multiple projects with a focus on furniture planning, building a strong conceptual strategy for the project that is rooted in the client’s vision and aspirations.\nGuides and motivates teams, leads the creative process, and promotes firm strategies, policies, and procedures.\nExpected to conceptualize, set direction for design, with a focus on furniture planning, and oversee production and discipline coordination.\nLead the interior design approach of the project’s goals through all phases of the project (the Pursuit, Programming and Visioning, Concept Design, Schematic Design, Design Development, Construction Design, Procurement and Construction Administration).\nEvaluate client needs, analyze and effectively document design objectives and spatial requirements.\nCoordinate and delegate project design work and code compliance.\nCollaborate work with other disciplines, including architecture, engineering, strategy, experiential branding and consultants.\nConduct a review of drawings and support functions in conformance with project time, budget and quality constraints.\nDelegation and oversight of and production of design visualization.\nCollaborate with project leaders to develop project work plans for the interior design components of the project and monitor design staff adherence to schedule.\nLead client meetings and maintain strong client relationships.\nImplement, follow, maintain, and enforce interior design standards used throughout interior design team in all project aspects/phases.\nLead the development of and/or oversee documentation for furniture, fixtures, and equipment (FFE) throughout all phases of the interior furniture design work, as required.\nLead the development of material palettes that communicate stories and support the client’s objectives\nSpecification oversight.\nMentor and guide less experienced interior design staff.\nActively participate and promote design excellence and firm strategies.\nCollaborate with design leadership and participate in business development opportunities, and industry events\nConsult with furniture manufacturers, dealers, product vendors and industry partners, building strong relationships in the design community.\nLead and/or participate in marketing activities, including proposal development and interviews.\nParticipate in construction administration activities, including site visits, review of submittals and shop drawings, and conducting punch lists. Site visits frequently require a physical walk-through of site.\nEnsure sustainability metrics goals are met for projects.\nWork within project budgets and schedules to meet profitability goals.\nMaintain 80% billable time and 10% marketing time."}, {"h": "HERE'S WHAT YOU'LL NEED", "t": "Bachelor or Master's degree in Interior Design, Interior Architecture, or relevant field required.\nA minimum of 10 years of related experience is required.\nCurrent NCIDQ certification or applicable certification/licensure preferred.\nAbility to provide interior design leadership focusing on furniture across multiple projects.\nStrong experiential design, storytelling and technical skills as well as the knowledge of building and life safety codes required.\nExceptional presentation, organizational, team building, collaboration and communication skills are a must.\nThe ability to build and maintain client relationships is essential.\nExperience leading a high performing team and mentoring staff is required.\nConceptualization and ability to set direction for furniture planning, furniture palettes, specifications and implementation.\nApplication of standards and quality process adherence.\nProduction oversight and discipline coordination.\nCritical thinker and highly analytical.\nMust be a fully qualified professional able to perform work with a high degree of self-motivation, autonomy and strategic influence.\nProficiency with Revit, Enscape, Bluebeam, Microsoft Office, and Adobe Creative Suite required.\nTravel as required.\nThe salary range for this position is $98,328 to $122,933 annually. This salary range is the range we believe is the anticipated range of possible base compensation at the timing of the posting. We may ultimately pay more or less than the anticipated salary range for the position. Employees may be eligible for discretionary bonuses.\n\nWe offer a full benefit package including medical, dental and vision coverage and flexible spending account options and voluntary insurances. We have paid time off, flex-time schedules, remote work options and a 401k plan and employee perk programs.\n\nFor a general overview of our benefits, please visit our careers page at https://www.cannondesign.com/careers/benefits . Actual compensation may vary from posting based on geographic location, work experience, education and/or skill level."}, {"h": "ABOUT OUR FIRM", "t": "CannonDesign is a design practice where strategy, experience, architecture, engineering, and social impact converge. We don’t just dream up solutions — we create and bring them to life in ways to solve some of the biggest challenges facing our clients and the society.\n\nAt the heart of everything we do is Living-Centered Design, a bold commitment to using our talents to not just improve the world but to truly reshape it for the better. It’s more than a philosophy — it’s who we are, and it drives us to make a meaningful, lasting difference every day."}, {"h": "ABOUT WORKING HERE", "t": "We are relentless in our pursuit of client adoration (not simply satisfaction). Consistent delivery of the best service is what we are about.\nWe are committed to ensuring our practice provides equal opportunities for all employees, as we strive to connect with communities around us and focus on the future of design. We support equity, diversity, and inclusion efforts that benefit all employees through the leadership of our DEI Council, our Employee Resource Groups which are open to everyone, and other community initiatives.\nWe’re about communication and transparency here. If you want to talk to someone about an idea you have, or a challenge that needs addressing, we’re ready for you."}], "k": ["account-management", "bluebeam", "branding", "building-codes", "business-development", "cad-drafting", "community-engagement", "construction-administration", "enscape", "ffe", "furniture-design", "grant-writing", "materials", "procurement", "revit", "sustainability", "training", "writing"], "b": ["generous-pto", "vision"], "r": {"exp": 10, "edu": {"level": "bachelor", "state": "required"}}}, "21c7be9043": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "Zur Verstärkung unseres Teams suchen wir per sofort oder nach Vereinbarung eine engagierte, motivierte und teamfähige Persönlichkeit für unsere exklusiven Projekte im In- und Ausland für die Standorte Zürich oder St. Moritz\n**Innenarchitekt/In - (w/m) 100%**\nin Zürich und St. Moritz\nin unbefristeter Anstellung und in Vollzeit\n**Ihr Profil:**\nZuständigkeit für die Konzeption und das Design von Innenarchitekturprojekten\nKreativität und technisches Know-how in vielseitigen Bauprojekten\nErfolgreich abgeschlossenes Architektur/Designstudium\nMehrjährige Berufserfahrung\nSehr gute Kenntnisse im 3D Aufbau\nLösungsorientierte, zielstrebige Arbeitsweise\nKreativ, teamfähig, belastbar, zuverlässig\n**Wir bieten Ihnen **\nEine gut dotierte Dauerstelle an attraktivem Standort\nEinen modernen Arbeitsplatz in einem jungen Team\nMitarbeit an anspruchsvollen und interessanten Aufgaben\nMöglichkeit zum Aufstieg innerhalb unserer Firma\nWir freuen uns über Ihre aussagekräftige Bewerbung mit möglichem Eintrittstermin.\nKüchel Architects AG St. Moritz Zürich\nFrau Carla Salis-Testa\nVia Mulin 10\nCH-7500 St. Moritz\nwww.kuechelarchitects.ch\nsalis@kuechelarchitects.ch\nKontakt\nCarla Salis-Testa\nTel.: +41 81 725 00 00\nsalis@kuechelarchitects.ch\nAnbieter\nKüchel Architects\nVia Mulin 10\n7500 St. Moritz\nSwitzerland\nwww.kuechelarchitects.ch\n--------------------\nJobkategorie\nArchitekt\nArbeitsort\nZürich / St. Moritz\nDatum\n9. September\nArt der Beschäftigung\nVollzeit"}], "k": []}, "710d9e7754": {"s": [{"h": null, "t": "producing